      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "And as a “compromise”, it seems like they could limit it in quite a few ways and still provide the testing functionality.\n\nThings like providing only a single test sticker, only works when solo, drone is missing some features(?), etc.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-03-27T01:37:32.067Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There are varying opinions regarding the features such as Stickers and Drones in the Live version, but I understand that this is part of VRChat’s official direction. Layers have been provided to restrict the use of these features, and I believe it is possible to take preventative measures in areas where potential issues may arise.\n\nHowever, I do feel there is a concern regarding the fact that some of these features are limited exclusively to VRCPlus members. The reason being that creators who are not subscribed to VRCPlus are unable to test or verify the functionality of these features in their own worlds before releasing them.\n\nPersonally, I am a VRCPlus subscriber and therefore not affected by this limitation. However, many of my acquaintances who are also world creators are not subscribed. In light of this, would it be possible to consider implementing a temporary exemption—such as a ‘test Stickers’ mechanism—that allows creators to use these features in their own worlds solely for testing purposes?\n\nThank you very much for your consideration.",
